 ritual, drama, literature, and mythology. The world as forum for action is=
 a place of value, a place where all things have meaning. This meaning, whi=
ch is shaped as a consequence of social interaction, is implication for act=
ion, or=E2=80=94at a higher level of analysis=E2=80=94implication for the c=
onfiguration of the interpretive schema that produces or guides action. <br=
><br>The latter manner of interpretation=E2=80=94the world as place of thin=
gs=E2=80=94finds its formal expression in the methods and theories of scien=
ce. Science allows for increasingly precise determination of the consensual=
ly-validatable properties of things, and for efficient utilization of preci=
